explanation:
Dot notation is the usual choice: user.name. It works only when the key is a plain word you can write ahead of time.

Bracket notation takes an expression instead: settings[key]. It is the tool for keys that arrive as variables, come out of a form, or are not valid words.

Both forms read the same value, and both give undefined when the key is missing. When undefined is not a useful answer, supply a default on the same line: const theme = settings[key] ?? "light";

